-> A merged run (`kronikol merge`) writes its own `TestRunReport.html` and `TestRunReport.json` — see
+> A merged run (`kronikol merge`) writes its own `TestRunReport.html` and data file (`TestRunReport.krkl` when any input is one); see
 > [Merging Parallel Reports](Merging-Parallel-Reports).
 
 > **Data format:** `Specifications` data defaults to `.yml` (`SpecificationsDataFormat`); `TestRunReport` data defaults to `.json` (`TestRunReportDataFormat`). Set either to `DataFormat.Json`, `DataFormat.Yaml` or `DataFormat.Xml` to change it.
 
-> **File names:** All file names are configurable via `HtmlSpecificationsFileName`, `HtmlTestRunReportFileName`, and `YamlSpecificationsFileName` on `ReportConfigurationOptions`. A `kronikol query` given a folder finds a `TestRunReport.json` and nothing else, so with a custom `HtmlTestRunReportFileName` every command the run prints, and every command in `Failures.md`, names the data file itself (`kronikol query failures Checkout.json`; `Failures.md` since 4.20.6).
+> **File names:** All file names are configurable via `HtmlSpecificationsFileName`, `HtmlTestRunReportFileName`, and `YamlSpecificationsFileName` on `ReportConfigurationOptions`. A `kronikol query` given a folder finds a `.krkl` of any name, but a JSON data file only when its name ends `TestRunReport.json`, so with a custom `HtmlTestRunReportFileName` every command the run prints, and every command in `Failures.md`, names the data file itself (`kronikol query failures Checkout.krkl`; `Failures.md` since 4.20.6).
 
